WEBVTT

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:08.980
Sheesh.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.510
Give me a break already.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:13.990
Are you okay?

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.030
No, of course I'm not...

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.360
So cold!

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:24.700
Come on. Try some.

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:26.770
I can feed myself.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:30.380
That's good.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.050
Leader, would you like some?

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.950
No, I'll pass.

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.430
That looks good.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.560
The medium rare looks just about right.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.060
Yeah.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:42.940
I wish I could stuff myself full of that.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.060
Apparently, it's A5 beef.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.580
Do you want to go get some 
together after today's festival?

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.320
Well, actually...

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:52.090
Come eat with me, then.

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:53.000
What?

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.820
You worked hard at yesterday's rehearsal.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:59.200
Y-Yesterday's rehearsal 
certainly was perfect...

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.830
You thought our rehearsal was perfect?

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:03.660
Mikado-san.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.830
What does "perfect" mean 
for B-Pro, anyway?

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:12.460
I'm not sure how to put it, 
but you were all shining so brightly.

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:16.680
I'm sure other people will think 
it's amazing when they see it, too.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:19.470
Hey, Tsubasa-chan!

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:19.470
Huh?

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:23.710
Tsubasa-chan, join us!

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:24.250
When did they get there?

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:27.600
His head's always in the clouds.

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:29.740
Want to go over there?

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:31.070
Okay.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.090
Ryu-chan, help me pedal.

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:39.120
I can't. I said I didn't mind riding, 
but I wouldn't pedal.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:42.120
Tsubasa, your phone is blinking.

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:43.620
Huh?

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:44.870
<b>Yashamaru Sakutaro
Did something happen?!
What's wrong?
Tsubasa-chan
What are you doing?
It's way past time
Where are you?
Where's everyone from B-Pro?
What are you doing?
Tsubasa-chan
Hurry and get here
Tsubasa-chan
Where are you?</b>

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.860
What? It's Yashamaru-san.

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:48.670
I wonder what's going on.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.750
<i>What are you doing?!</i>

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:54.290
Um, sightseeing with the guys?

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:56.450
<i>You're late! You're really, really late!</i>

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:57.120
What?

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.300
<i>I told you to be here at nine!</i>

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.390
What? I thought it was at eleven.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:05.790
<i>That was rehearsal! Are you trying 
to embarrass Nishiyama-san?</i>

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.970
N-No! I'm sorry!

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.730
G-Guys, I'm sorry!

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:14.180
We need to get to the 
event space immediately!

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:16.060
What?

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:47.950
<b>RAIZIN ROCK FES</b>

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:57.130
I-In any case, let's hurry!

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:01.800
Please accept this gift!

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:03.300
Oh, it's not Omens.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:04.790
Who are they?

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:07.010
Some idol group called Kitakore, I think.

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:13.770
Today, we're appearing as 
part of B-Project. I hope you like it.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:16.020
Oh, okay.

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:21.590
Sumisora-san, let's hurry.

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:22.990
R-Right.

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:26.250
So, where should we go?

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:29.620
Um... this way.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:33.120
We're here. Wait here, please.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:34.920
The lighting room?

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.140
I don't know how to work the lights.

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:38.840
I'm sorry!

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:40.300
This is it!

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.430
The merchandise booth?

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:44.800
Star Curry is now on sale!

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:47.870
It's actually here!

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:52.430
What?

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:56.490
I see. Tsubasa, are you trying 
to say you want to get in with me?

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:58.190
N-No.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:00.860
I'm so sorry. I'm so sorry!

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:03.150
You're still out here?

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:04.640
Yashamaru-san.

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:07.130
I had them push back your rehearsal a bit.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:09.320
Boys, get on stage right now.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:10.370
Got it!

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:18.330
You're going to come apologize 
to everyone with me.

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:21.340
O-Okay...

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:23.840
<b>RAIZIN ROCK FES</b>

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:28.820
Okay, next up is...

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:30.010
Sorry we're late.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:33.950
We're B-Project. We look 
forward to working with you.

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:35.620
You're late.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:36.970
We're terribly sorry.

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:39.490
Anyway, let's get this rehearsal started.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.140
Thank you.

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:57.000
Noise?

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:00.420
I can't hear our audio.

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:02.380
Huh? Did you say something?

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.630
Move this, please.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:07.630
Not over there.

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:08.550
Where do you want it?

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:09.640
Yeah, right there.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:16.890
Could we stop for a second?

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:21.980
Is something wrong?

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:26.550
Has the stage changed 
since yesterday's rehearsal?

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:29.250
What? Yashamaru-san didn't tell you?

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:32.100
No. We just met up with him earlier.

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:35.290
Really? Well, we're going 
to be leaving equipment here

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:38.220
during the first half for a scene change.

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:42.670
The space may be a little smaller now. 
But you're fine, right?

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:49.220
I hate to say this, but we don't have much 
time to rehearse since you guys were late.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:50.930
You'll have to rehearse like this.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:54.170
If we can't use this area, 
then MooNs' space—

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:56.430
It's all right. We'll manage.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:06:58.430
Leader?

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:01.130
But yesterday's rehearsal formation—

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:04.310
This kind of thing happens 
all the time. We can handle it.

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:07.180
Either way's fine with me, 
but we're running out of time.

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:08.400
Are you rehearsing again?

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.570
Yes. We'll change our formation and—

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:12.000
We've rehearsed plenty already.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.030
We'll see you during the live performance.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:16.450
Kazu?

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:20.500
Why did our rehearsal time change?

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:24.110
One of the performing groups arrived late.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:25.750
Is that them?

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.340
Probably.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.470
What's going on? 
They look like they're fighting.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:34.490
Apparently, Nishiyama-san 
recommended them.

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:37.470
Really? What's so great about them?

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.740
This is why I hate handsome guys.

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:42.940
A mask is better than a handsome face.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.860
That's right.

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:57.330
I'm sorry, everyone!

00:07:58.070 --> 00:07:59.260
Don't worry about it.

00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:02.100
Tsubasa-chan, did you get in lots of trouble?

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:04.760
Yes, lots of trouble.

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:06.500
Don't worry about it.

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:07.670
Kazu.

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:12.010
I was just thinking in the anteroom.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:16.750
For the "Kodo Ambitious" formation, 
I think MooNs should be...

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:19.010
I said that's not necessary.

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:22.990
We'll solve our own problems ourselves.

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:27.680
D-Did something happen?

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:30.300
There was a little trouble 
at the rehearsal just now.

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:31.940
Hey, Masunaga.

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:37.700
You're acting like it's MooNs' problem, 
but we were invited here as B-Pro.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.700
There's no point in putting on 
a self-satisfying performance.

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:42.180
Goshi.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.240
I will follow my leader.

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:50.040
In the first place, no one's paying much 
attention to B-Pro's performances.

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:52.210
Th-That's not true!

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:56.070
We were kicked out of the FMJ
Song Festival, too.

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:57.650
That was...

00:08:57.650 --> 00:08:58.850
You're right.

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:05.430
Maybe so, but I wanted to rehearse 
a little more. I couldn't hear our audio at all.

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:10.650
Yeah, it was hard to sing. Maybe 
that's normal for this kind of festival.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.970
The text on the prompters was wrong, too.

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:16.110
The staff doesn't take us seriously.

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:18.940
The ear monitors were 
making noise the whole time.

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:24.040
Sorry. If only I'd done a better job...

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:26.550
That's not what we're talking about, Tsubasa.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:29.820
Guys, look!

00:09:31.990 --> 00:09:34.410
Hamburgers and baumkuchen.

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:36.890
Ugh. I don't even want to think 
of all the calories in those.

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.500
They were at the catering area.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.470
Why don't you guys have some?

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:45.440
Come to think of it, we missed 
our chance to eat Omi beef.

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:47.690
Maybe I'll get something to eat, too.

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:49.880
Leader, let's go.

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:52.940
What? Oh, sure.

00:09:58.390 --> 00:10:00.300
I'll make some coffee.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:06.620
Have you heard of B-Whatever?

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:09.740
Yeah, the guys who were recommended.

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:14.310
I can't believe they showed up late to 
rehearsal and then complained about the stage.

00:10:14.310 --> 00:10:16.370
Seriously, I know.

00:10:16.370 --> 00:10:21.340
Besides, I'm opposed to idols appearing 
on RAIZIN in the first place.

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:25.310
Huh? Why are you winking?

00:10:26.410 --> 00:10:29.550
Hey, didn't you say you 
don't like idols, either?

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:32.800
No, I don't think I ever said that.

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:34.350
You liar.

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:36.590
Anyway, I think those B-Whatever guys are—

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:38.530
What about B-Whatever?

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:41.390
Hey, the Whatevers.

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:45.250
If you've got something to say, 
we'll hear you out.

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:48.540
It's not like I don't.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:49.450
What?

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:54.510
You may have been recommended, 
but you were late to rehearsal.

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:56.050
You complained about the stage.

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:58.800
Can you even sing a proper song?

00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:00.400
What did you say?

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:04.300
We're just trying to give the best 
performance possible in the space

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:05.530
that's been provided.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:12.650
You just look like spoiled brats to me.

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:13.690
You bastard!

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:16.570
Goshi!

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:21.060
I-I'm sorry! Are you all right?

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:23.410
We're fine.

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:25.790
Good.

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:27.530
But our costumes...

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:38.760
The concert's about to begin, too.

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:43.340
<b>Starts in</b>

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:46.030
What do the guidelines say?

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:47.490
Rain or shine, we're going on.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:49.350
Let's go.

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:53.060
Absolutely not!

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:55.530
Don't be that way, Anzu-chan.

00:11:55.530 --> 00:11:57.320
We have to perform, rain or shine.

00:11:57.590 --> 00:12:00.920
You can't call a storm like this "rain."

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:03.150
Besides, my makeup will run.

00:12:03.150 --> 00:12:05.250
And the stage will be slippery.

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:07.930
Yeah, but it's already starting.

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:10.540
Excuse me, but they're not ready yet.

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:16.100
Omens. Omens, can you go on?

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:17.710
In this rain?

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:20.690
No one else is willing to perform.

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:22.720
We can't play our instruments.

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:26.920
Besides, when our masks get wet, 
we don't have any power.

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:28.970
Yeah, that's right.

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:32.230
Sheesh, what's their problem?

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:34.870
What's going to happen?

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:36.730
It's really coming down.

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:39.530
What are you boys doing?

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:42.030
We came to see the opening act.

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:44.780
Huh? Where's Tsubasa-chan?

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:48.910
There's been a... problem.

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:51.740
It's still not starting?

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:53.360
Well, just look at this rain.

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:55.860
Nishiyama-san?

00:12:55.860 --> 00:13:00.910
It's no wonder no one's excited about 
performing under these circumstances.

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:02.250
It's only natural.

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:09.350
Nishiyama-san...

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:13.890
Yeah, I have to go on.

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:18.670
Even under these circumstances, 
the fans are still waiting for us.

00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:22.440
The fans, huh?

00:13:24.810 --> 00:13:26.280
Those girls...

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:31.210
We'll go.

00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:33.880
Kitakado-kun?

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:36.520
If this rain were enough to stop us,

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:38.580
we wouldn't be able to perform 
even under clear skies.

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:40.580
I agree.

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:42.100
Kazu.

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:50.850
Nishiyama-san, would it be 
all right if we performed?

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:55.100
Sure, I don't mind.

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:58.340
Of course. Can you go on soon?

00:13:58.340 --> 00:13:59.100
Yeah!

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:02.070
But what about Ryu-chan's costume?

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:05.860
Almost there...

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:08.400
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:11.740
It's show time! B-Project!

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:12.200
Huh?

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:14.260
What? What? What?

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:15.700
What?!

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:20.290
Yes!

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:22.170
Kitakado-san!

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:22.170
B-Pro!

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:24.880
We are B-Project!

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:27.250
Here we go, everyone!

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:29.890
Kitakore is up first!

00:14:31.060 --> 00:14:38.980
<i>Fragile like the stars and sad like the moon</i>

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:49.170
<i>I'll always illuminate 
only you from this place</i>

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:57.700
<i>I want to protect that somehow 
sad and downcast smile</i>

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:52.660
Wasn't my plan surprisingly good?

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:55.410
I call it B-Project: Naked!

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:57.700
It's got a lot of impact.

00:14:57.700 --> 00:15:04.590
<i>I just want to look at you</i>

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:08.470
We're THRIVE!

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:11.470
We won't let Kitakore beat us!

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:14.720
Enjoy our superb singing and dancing.

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:26.110
<i>Beyond the future, let's create 
a shining era of ascension</i>

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:31.490
<i>We'll continue moving straight forward</i>

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:38.620
<i>So we don't miss the dream that's 
endlessly spreading out before us now</i>

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:42.370
<i>We'll pick up the pieces 
and put them together</i>

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:50.340
<i>Even the smallest lights someday</i>

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.060
We are MooNs!

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:55.630
Thanks for waiting!

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:57.180
Let's get pumped up.

00:15:57.180 --> 00:16:00.330
We'll blow this rain away!

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:03.190
Tatsu, that's a cool thing to say.

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:11.950
<i>If you turn around, you'll always see</i>

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:18.540
<i>The footprints we've left behind</i>

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:22.540
<i>When I was about to break</i>

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:28.960
<i>You simply held out your hand</i>

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:33.270
The sky...

00:16:33.270 --> 00:16:35.220
The costume is ready.

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:39.930
Hurry! Get ready for a quick change.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:50.680
Finally, "Kodo Ambitious!"

00:16:56.360 --> 00:17:03.000
<i>(I...) Thousands of coincidences 
(feel...) brought us together</i>

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:09.170
<i>(You...) The moment we met 
(now...) our DESTINY began to move</i>

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:10.840
<i>Say Never give it up</i>

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:12.460
<i>Don't hesitate</i>

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:14.090
<i>We must going on</i>

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:15.720
<i>Believe</i>

00:17:15.940 --> 00:17:22.430
<i>Those single-minded eyes 
shine with a blinding light</i>

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:26.350
<i>With certain feelings, we create</i>

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:34.280
<i>With both hands, grab onto a limitless future</i>

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:42.360
<i>Everything will be changed 
into a brand-new world</i>

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:39.780
I'm glad I recommended B-Project.

00:17:40.180 --> 00:17:41.660
Thank you.

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:45.040
They took the best part, though.

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:49.040
<i>If you dive in, I'll be waiting 
there right by your side</i>

00:17:45.390 --> 00:17:47.650
You wanted to go on, didn't you?

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:55.590
<i>Everything can be changed 
in our very own Story</i>

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:57.320
Things will start to get tough for them now.

00:17:55.590 --> 00:18:05.990
<i>A beating ambition like no one's 
ever seen that pounds for tomorrow</i>

00:17:57.800 --> 00:18:03.350
Yes, but those boys still 
have a lot up their sleeves.

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:08.370
But I'm sure they'll be able to enjoy it.

00:18:05.990 --> 00:18:12.360
<i>The unstoppable pounding 
of my heart tingles and throbs</i>

00:18:10.760 --> 00:18:12.360
You might be right.

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:19.200
<i>And when it overflows with heart-pounding 
excitement, we'll advance to the next stage</i>

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:32.200
Good work.

00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:33.320
Good work.

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:34.370
Good work.

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:35.740
Good work.

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:35.740
Good work.

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:36.520
Good work.

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:38.790
Ba-dump! That was a great concert.

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:38.260
Good work.

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:40.140
It was superb.

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:42.070
You made it.

00:18:42.070 --> 00:18:44.650
Yeah, just barely.

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:47.360
I feel like you were just 
barely too late, though.

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:49.100
Sorry.

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:53.120
Kaneshiro-san, here.

00:18:53.890 --> 00:18:56.990
We were awesome today.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.590
Yeah, you're right.

00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:01.680
What's wrong, Goshi?

00:19:02.810 --> 00:19:04.520
You still got a problem with us?

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:08.480
You were pretty decent.

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:40.240
Tsubasa.

00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:42.620
What's wrong?

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:45.230
I was just thinking.

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:48.870
B-Pro really is amazing.

00:19:49.610 --> 00:19:53.690
I was thinking that I want even 
more people see you perform.

00:19:54.380 --> 00:20:01.400
Yeah, but even if we think we're amazing, 
B-Pro doesn't have nearly enough exposure.

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:04.680
It always comes back to that.

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:06.390
That's our problem for the time being.

00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:09.020
You're right.

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:12.660
If only they'd watch us perform...

00:20:12.660 --> 00:20:17.520
Then we'd probably 
at least make it to the Dome.

00:20:19.210 --> 00:20:20.440
The Dome?

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:23.030
That would be great.

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:25.690
A solo B-Project performance at the Dome...

00:20:25.690 --> 00:20:26.910
Let's aim for that.

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:32.410
Why are you laughing?

00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:35.150
Oh, sorry.

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:38.750
You're right. We should dream big.

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:42.260
I actually think we could make it.

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:45.340
Well, we do have a lot of big problems.

00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:48.350
But I'd like to go to the Dome.

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:50.530
Why not?

00:20:50.530 --> 00:20:52.810
I feel like we just might be able to.

00:20:53.360 --> 00:20:54.960
Sounds interesting.

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:58.060
All right! Let's aim for the Dome!

00:20:58.390 --> 00:21:01.030
Good work, boys.

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:02.850
Yashamaru-san.

00:21:02.850 --> 00:21:07.440
Tsubasa-chan, you had me 
really scared this time.

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:09.910
I'm really sorry.

00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:14.870
It turned out to be a huge 
success, so it's fine.

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:17.900
But from now on, make sure 
you check the start time.

00:21:17.900 --> 00:21:18.770
Okay.

00:21:18.770 --> 00:21:24.250
But you must be really clumsy 
to have mixed up nine and eleven.

00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:24.850
What?

00:21:25.290 --> 00:21:27.260
Maybe there was another reason.

00:21:27.480 --> 00:21:31.400
What does that mean? 
Are you saying I made a mistake?

00:21:31.400 --> 00:21:34.230
Oh, please. I would never...

00:21:35.800 --> 00:21:37.270
You just gasped!

00:21:37.490 --> 00:21:40.270
No, I...

00:21:40.270 --> 00:21:41.900
<b>Starts at 11</b>

00:21:40.560 --> 00:21:41.900
Hey, wait!

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:45.010
Tsubasa-chan, look at this.

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:51.410
Uh, well... Tsubasa-chan...

00:21:52.030 --> 00:21:56.040
I'll treat you to whatever 
you want. Don't hold back.

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:57.860
What? But I don't—

00:21:57.860 --> 00:21:58.750
Omi beef!

00:21:58.750 --> 00:21:59.830
What?

00:21:59.830 --> 00:22:02.250
Special A5 Omi steaks!

00:22:02.660 --> 00:22:04.660
Thanks for the food!

00:22:06.220 --> 00:22:08.970
What?!

00:23:40.610 --> 00:23:41.850
Yeah, it's me.

00:23:43.160 --> 00:23:45.960
I see. So it's coming along well?

00:23:48.120 --> 00:23:51.860
Yeah, I'm counting on you. 
Move things along like we planned.

00:23:55.780 --> 00:23:57.750
It's such a waste to go to sleep.

00:23:57.750 --> 00:23:59.350
Can I squeeze you?
